From: lichenggang <lichenggang@uniontech.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 17:38:28 +0800
Subject: Restore legacy X11 cursor name aliases

Adwaita 48.1 dropped the legacy X11 cursor names that window
managers and toolkits still request (size_all, size_ver, size_hor,
size_bdiag, size_fdiag, openhand, closedhand, ibeam, left_ptr_watch,
pointing_hand, forbidden, split_v, split_h, whats_this, dnd-copy,
dnd-link and the old X11 cursor hash names). deepin's kwin for
example requests size_all while moving a window, so the cursor no
longer switches to the grabbing hand when dragging a window.
Restore these names as install-time symlinks pointing to the
corresponding Adwaita cursors.

Signed-off-by: lichenggang <lichenggang@uniontech.com>
---
--- a/meson.build	2026-08-17 17:38:22.769269099 +0800
+++ b/meson.build	2026-08-17 17:38:22.778269246 +0800
@@ -48,28 +48,59 @@
